# =====================================================================
# NYU CSCI-GA.2433 Database Systems - course project
#
# What belongs in the repository: source, schema, models, documentation,
# diagrams, reports, and the evidence the report cites.
#
# What does not: credentials, re-downloadable public data, packaging
# output, run logs, caches, and personal working notes. Everything
# excluded here is either regenerable by a script in this repository or
# has no value to a reader of the project.
# =====================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Credentials. Never committed, under any circumstances.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*_key.json
*-key.json
service-account*.json
credentials*.json
gcloud-*.json
.pgpass

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Raw and intermediate data: 300 MB of public downloads.
#
# Restore with:
#   cd part2_data_lake
#   python3 scripts/download_part2_data.py
#   python3 scripts/01_inventory_data.py
#   python3 scripts/02_profile_data.py
#   python3 scripts/03_build_curated_data.py
#
# metadata/download_manifest.json records each source URL and its
# expected SHA-256, so a restored file can be verified against the bytes
# the project was built on. The small curated/ and metadata/ outputs the
# loaders actually need are committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
part2_data_lake/raw/
part2_data_lake/processed/
part2_data_lake/sample_data/

# Retraining fixtures, ~21 MB, derived from the DS010 report.
# Rebuild with: python3 part4/tests/fixtures/make_fixtures.py
part4/tests/fixtures/*.pdf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Packaging output. Archives are built by scripts; the reports they
#    contain are committed on their own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
part2_data_lake/submission/
part4/submission/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Run logs and personal working notes. Neither is project software.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
*.out
*.pid
part2_data_lake/project_work/
part2_data_lake/validation/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Not part of this project.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
HW/
Lecture/
Mo_p3_su26/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Caches and editor or OS noise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Implementation diaries, planning notes, and inventories.
#
# These were working aids while the parts were being built. The design
# decisions worth keeping are in docs/design_decisions.md and
# docs/limitations.md; the requirement mappings that matter are in the
# traceability matrices. A reader of the finished project needs neither
# the command log nor the pre-work inventory.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
part2_data_lake/docs/execution_log.md
part2_data_lake/docs/part3_implementation_plan.md
part2_data_lake/docs/part3_repository_inventory.md
part2_data_lake/part3/

# A restated copy of the assignment brief is not project software.
**/PART3_REQUIREMENTS.md

# The Part II report is committed as .docx and .md; the PDF is the same
# document in a third format.
part2_data_lake/report/Project_Part2_Report.pdf

# Word lock files
~$*
